# katgpt-web local environment — the template for `.env` (gitignored, NEVER commit).
#
# Copy:  cp .env.example .env   then uncomment what you need.
# Nothing here auto-loads .env: `vite.config.js` reads `process.env` directly
# (Vite's own .env loading only populates `import.meta.env` for client code,
# and this repo reads none). Export the vars, or load the file first:
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a; npm run build
#
# This repo reads NO credentials or secrets. The only config knob is the
# Vite base path below.

# ── Vite build (vite.config.js) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_BASE: public base path assets are served from.
#   Default: '/katgpt-web/' when GITHUB_ACTIONS is set (GitHub Pages project
#   page, .github/workflows/deploy.yml), otherwise '/'. Override if your
#   repo / Pages path differs.
# VITE_BASE=/
